You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics shipment tracker. The project is already scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-6ac0ea3fbb26414ea75aab96306f1a8e/ShipmentTracker/` with Interactive Auto Global mode and Individual authentication.

## What to do:

### 1. Create AGENTS.md in the server project root (`/tmp/sv-6ac0ea3fbb26414ea75aab96306f1a8e/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/AGENTS.md`) with this content (replace {AppName} with ShipmentTracker):

```
# ShipmentTracker

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| **Interactivity Mode** | Auto |
| **Interactivity Scope** | Global |

## Rendering configuration
This project uses global Interactive Auto with prerendering.
Created with `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`.

On a user's first visit, components render via Interactive Server (SignalR). On subsequent visits the cached WebAssembly runtime takes over and interactions run entirely in the browser.

## Authentication
ASP.NET Core Identity is configured with Individual accounts. Identity pages under `Components/Account/` are always static SSR — do not add `@rendermode` to them.

## Project structure
- **ShipmentTracker** (server): Hosts the Blazor app, serves static files, API endpoints.
- **ShipmentTracker.Client** (WebAssembly): All interactive UI components. Run on server first, then browser.

## Adding new components
- Interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project, not the server project.
- New pages go in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`.
- All pages are already interactive (global mode). No need to add `@rendermode` to individual components.
- Server-only static components (e.g., error pages) belong in the server `Components/` folder.

## Data access
Interactive components cannot access the database directly. Use this pattern:
1. Define an interface in the `.Client` project (e.g., `IDataService`).
2. In the `.Client` project, implement it using `HttpClient` to call server APIs.
3. In the server project, implement it using direct data access (EF Core DbContext, etc.).
4. Register the client implementation in the client `Program.cs` and the server implementation in the server `Program.cs`.
5. Expose server data through minimal API endpoints (e.g., `app.MapGet(...)`) that the client implementation calls.
6. If the page requires authorization, apply the same auth policy to both the Blazor page (`@attribute [Authorize]`) and the minimal API endpoint (`.RequireAuthorization()`).

## Service registration
- Both server and client `Program.cs` must register matching services for any DI used by interactive components.
- Server-only services (EF Core, Identity) stay in the server `Program.cs` only.

## Don'ts
- Don't put interactive components in the server project — they work during prerender but fail after WebAssembly handoff.
- Don't inject `DbContext` or server-only services in `.Client` project components — use HTTP APIs instead.
- Don't assume execution environment — the same component runs on Server first, then WebAssembly later.
- Don't add `@rendermode` to pages — global interactivity is already configured in `App.razor`.
- Don't add `@rendermode` to Identity/Account pages — they must stay static SSR.
```

### 2. Delete default template pages
Delete these files from the Client project:
- `/tmp/sv-6ac0ea3fbb26414ea75aab96306f1a8e/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Counter.razor`
- `/tmp/sv-6ac0ea3fbb26414ea75aab96306f1a8e/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Weather.razor`

### 3. Create shared models in the Client project

Create `/tmp/sv-6ac0ea3fbb26414ea75aab96306f1a8e/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### 4. Create the service interface in the Client project

Create `/tmp/sv-6ac0ea3fbb26414ea75aab96306f1a8e/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment);
    Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 5. Create client-side HTTP implementation

Create `/tmp/sv-6ac0ea3fbb26414ea75aab96306f1a8e/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient httpClient) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await httpClient.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>())!;
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var response = await httpClient.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>())!;
    }
}
```

### 6. Create the Dispatcher Shipments page

Create `/tmp/sv-6ac0ea3fbb26414ea75aab96306f1a8e/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Shipments.razor`:
```razor
@page "/shipments"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services
@attribute [Authorize]
@inject IShipmentService ShipmentService

<PageTitle>Shipments - Dispatcher Dashboard</PageTitle>

<h1>Shipment Dashboard</h1>

@if (_loading)
{
    <p><em>Loading shipments...</em></p>
}
else
{
    <div class="mb-3">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="ShowCreateForm">+ New Shipment</button>
    </div>

    @if (_showCreateForm)
    {
        <div class="card mb-3">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">Create New Shipment</h5>
                <div class="row g-2">
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <input class="form-control" placeholder="Origin" @bind="_newShipment.Origin" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <input class="form-control" placeholder="Destination" @bind="_newShipment.Destination" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <input class="form-control" placeholder="Customer Email" @bind="_newShipment.CustomerEmail" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <input class="form-control" placeholder="Description" @bind="_newShipment.Description" />
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-2">
                    <button class="btn btn-success btn-sm" @onclick="CreateShipment">Create</button>
                    <button class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" @onclick="() => _showCreateForm = false">Cancel</button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    }

    <table class="table table-striped">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Tracking #</th>
                <th>Origin</th>
                <th>Destination</th>
                <th>Status</th>
                <th>Est. Delivery</th>
                <th>Actions</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var shipment in _shipments)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td><code>@shipment.TrackingNumber</code></td>
                    <td>@shipment.Origin</td>
                    <td>@shipment.Destination</td>
                    <td><span class="badge @GetStatusBadgeClass(shipment.Status)">@shipment.Status</span></td>
                    <td>@shipment.EstimatedDelivery?.ToString("MMM dd, yyyy")</td>
                    <td>
                        <select class="form-select form-select-sm" style="width: auto; display: inline-block;"
                                value="@shipment.Status" @onchange="e => UpdateStatus(shipment, e)">
                            @foreach (var status in Enum.GetValues<ShipmentStatus>())
                            {
                                <option value="@status">@status</option>
                            }
                        </select>
                    </td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
}

@code {
    private List<Shipment> _shipments = [];
    private bool _loading = true;
    private bool _showCreateForm;
    private Shipment _newShipment = new();

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        _shipments = await ShipmentService.GetAllShipmentsAsync();
        _loading = false;
    }

    private void ShowCreateForm()
    {
        _showCreateForm = true;
        _newShipment = new Shipment();
    }

